        "procedure": "Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 mmol, 0.0456 g), 2-hydroxy-1-naphthaldehyde (0.2 mmol, 0.0344 g), 2-amino-2-methyl-propane-1,3-diol (0.1 mmol, 0.0105 g), acetonitrile (1.0 mL), methanol (0.5 mL) and ethanol (0.5 mL) were dissolved in a 20 cm Pyrex tube, then 30 mL of triethylamine was added. The tube was sealed under vacuum and heated at 80 °C for 6 h. After cooling to room temperature, light yellow crystals of 1 were obtained. Schiff-base ligands H3L1 and HL2 formed in situ.",
